# Mobile App Guidelines

## Stack
- Expo Router (`apps/app/app/`)
- Tab shell: `MainTabShell` + `MainTabNavProvider` — tab state must stay in sync with route path
- API client: `lib/api/*` — no raw fetch scattered in screens

## Structure
- `components/screens/` — tab/page screens
- `components/paw/` — design-system UI
- `context/` — global React context providers
- `hooks/` — reusable logic
- `lib/navigation/` — navigation helpers (e.g. `open-chat.ts`)

## Rules
- Minimal diffs; match existing styling (`constants/paw-styles`)
- Unread/state shared via context when multiple surfaces need it (tab bar + inbox)
- Opening chat: use `openChat(router, id, origin)`; exiting must restore correct tab route
- Env: `EXPO_PUBLIC_*` for API URL; production builds must not depend on Metro/LAN

## Keyboard + scroll (mandatory)
**Every screen or sheet that has a text input (where the software keyboard can appear) MUST have scrolling enabled.** Never use a non-scroll layout for input screens.

- Wrap the screen in `KeyboardAwareFormScroll` (or an equivalent scroll container that keeps `keyboardShouldPersistTaps` and still scrolls while the IME is open).
- Existing list screens that already use `ScrollView` / `FlatList` (feed, inbox, chat messages) must still remain scrollable with the keyboard open — add keyboard-sized bottom padding via `useKeyboardAwareBottomPadding` rather than freezing the layout.
- Bottom sheets with inputs (report, comments, filters, compose) must use the same pattern. Do not put a focused `TextInput` in a non-scroll parent.
- Prefer the shared wrapper over copy-pasted `KeyboardAvoidingView` per screen.

## Forbidden in screens
- Business rules that belong in API
- Duplicate WebSocket connections when a provider already handles events
- Input screens without a scroll container (see Keyboard + scroll)

## Tests
- Add tests for non-trivial hooks/utils when changing behavior (see 03-testing)
